  "final_message": "I haven't removed anything, because `channel` isn't unused.\n\n- **analytics-ingest needs it.** `analytics-ingest/src/core/events.ts:34` requires `channel` on `OrderPlaced`. Its README says a missing or unknown `channel` makes ingestion reject the event. It also writes `channel` to its `orders` table (`src/ingest.ts:17`). If orders-service stopped sending it, every `OrderPlaced` event would be rejected.\n- **orders-service reads it too.** `src/api/legacyExport.ts:6,18` exports it as a CSV column, and `test/adapters.test.ts:137` asserts that header.\n- **Clients send it.** `POST /orders` takes `channel` as input and validates it (`requestParsing.ts`, `order.ts:124`). Dropping it from the order model changes that documented API.\n- **billing-service tolerates its absence.** Its tests build events with `channel` undefined, so removing it wouldn't hurt billing.\n\nI can't edit the other teams' repos, since they're read-only here. Some ways forward:\n\n1. **Coordinate first.** Ask the analytics team to make `channel` optional or drop it, then remove it from orders-service afterwards.\n2. **Narrow change now.** Remove it from the `OrderPlaced` event only. This breaks analytics-ingest until they change, so I wouldn't do it before they're ready.\n3. **Full removal.** Remove it from the event, order model, request parsing, legacy export and tests. This only makes sense once the analytics change has shipped and the CSV consumers are confirmed.\n\nWhich do you want? If you know analytics-ingest is already being changed, tell me and I'll do option 3.",
